s are competent, it is not required that they\nremain unbiased."},"correctAnswer":"B","topic":"Audit Principles & Evidence","standard":"Philippine Standards on Auditing (PSA)","rationale":"Under auditing standards and professional practice, Option B accurately reflects the applicable requirement. The auditor gathers sufficient appropriate evidence to provide reasonable assurance regarding the relevant management assertions and financial statement disclosures.","distractorNotes":"The other choices are either inconsistent with Philippine auditing standards or represent incorrect procedures for this engagement stage."},{"id":"AT-100-48","set":"AT-100","num":48,"question":"Which of the following statement(s) is (are) true","options":{"A":"Gross negligence may constitute constructive fraud","B":"Constructive fraud is also termed recklessness","C":"Fraud requires the intent to deceive","D":"All the responses are true."},"correctAnswer":"D","topic":"Audit Principles & Evidence","standard":"Philippine Standards on Auditing (PSA)","rationale":"Under auditing standards and professional practice, Option D accurately reflects the applicable requirement. The auditor gathers sufficient appropriate evidence to provide reasonable assurance regarding the relevant management assertions and financial statement disclosures.","distractorNotes":"The other choices are either inconsistent with Philippine auditing standards or represent incorrect procedures for this engagement stage."},{"id":"AT-100-49","set":"AT-100","num":49,"question":"Which of the following is ordinarily true of a modification of the\naudit report by adding an emphasis of matter paragraph","options":{"A":"The modification by adding an emphasis of matter paragraph is an\n\"except for\" qualification of opinion","B":"The emphasis of matter paragraph is a \"subject to qualification of\nopinion","C":"The emphasis of matter paragraph would ordinarily refer to the fact\nthat the auditor's opinion is not qualified","D":"The emphasis of matter paragraph is presented before the opinion\nparagraph"},"correctAnswer":"C","topic":"Audit Opinions & Reports","standard":"PSA 700 / 705 / 706 (Auditor's Reports & Modifications)","rationale":"Under PSA 706, an Emphasis of Matter paragraph draws attention to a matter appropriately presented or disclosed in the financial statements that is fundamental to users' understanding. The auditor explicitly states that the opinion is NOT qualified in respect of the matter emphasized.","distractorNotes":"An emphasis of matter is not an 'except for' qualification, does not express a 'subject to' opinion (which is prohibited under auditing standards), and is placed immediately after the opinion paragraph."},{"id":"AT-100-50","set":"AT-100","num":50,"question":"Which of the following-statements is not true","options":{"A":"A one-paragraph report is generally used when the auditor is not\nindependent","B":"A modification of the audit report that involves modified wordings\nmay contain an unqualified opinion","C":"An addition of another paragraph to an otherwise standard audit report\nalways requires a modification of an unqualified opinion","D":"An unqualified opinion may be issued though the audit report requires\nan additional explanatory paragraph"},"correctAnswer":"C","topic":"Audit Principles & Evidence","standard":"Philippine Standards on Auditing (PSA)","rationale":"Under auditing standards and professional practice, Option C accurately reflects the applicable requirement. The auditor gathers sufficient appropriate evidence to provide reasonable assurance regarding the relevant management assertions and financial statement disclosures.","distractorNotes":"The other choices are either inconsistent with Philippine auditing standards or represent incorrect procedures for this engagement stage."},{"id":"AT-100-51","set":"AT-100","num":51,"question":"Which of the following-statements is not true","options":{"A":"A one-paragraph report is generally used when the auditor is not\nindependent","B":"A modification of the audit report that involves modified wordings\nmay contain an unqualified opinion","C":"An addition of another paragraph to an otherwise standard audit report\nalways requires a modification of an unqualified opinion","D":"An unqualified opinion may be issued though the audit report requires\nan additional explanatory paragraph"},"correctAnswer":"C","topic":"Audit Principles & Evidence","standard":"Philippine Standards on Auditing (PSA)","rationale":"Under auditing standards and professional practice, Option C accurately reflects the applicable requirement. The auditor gathers sufficient appropriate evidence to provide reasonable assurance regarding the relevant management assertions and financial statement disclosures.","distractorNotes":"The other choices are either inconsistent with Philippine auditing standards or represent incorrect procedures for this engagement stage."},{"id":"AT-100-52","set":"AT-100","num":52,"question":"Which of the following is not a true statement? \"In the opinion\nparagraph of the standard unqualified report, required to state","options":{"A":"an opinion about the financial statements taken as whole","B":"a conclusion about whether the company follows Philippine financial\nreporting standards","C":"whether the management has or has not made adequate disclosure","D":"That the financial statements are presented fairly."},"correctAnswer":"C","topic":"Audit Opinions & Reports","standard":"PSA 700 / 705 / 706 (Auditor's Reports & Modifications)","rationale":"Under PSA 700 and PSA 705, the auditor evaluates whether the financial statements are prepared, in all material respects, in accordance with the applicable financial reporting framework, determining whether an unmodified, qualified, adverse, or disclaimer of opinion is required.","distractorNotes":"The other choices confuse the circumstances of GAAP departure (qualified/adverse) with scope restrictions (qualified/disclaimer) or empha