s least likely create “self-interest\nthreat”","options":{"A":"Undue dependence on total fees from an assurance client","B":"Concern about the possibility of losing the engagement","C":"Having a close business relationship with an assurance client","D":"Pressure to reduce inappropriately the extent of work performed in\norder to reduce fees."},"correctAnswer":"D","topic":"Professional Ethics & Independence","standard":"Philippine Code of Ethics for Professional Accountants","rationale":"The Philippine Code of Ethics establishes five fundamental principles (Integrity, Objectivity, Professional Competence & Due Care, Confidentiality, and Professional Behavior) and a conceptual framework requiring CPAs to identify, evaluate, and address threats to compliance through appropriate safeguards.","distractorNotes":"Other choices either misclassify the threat category or propose actions that do not satisfy required ethical safeguards."},{"id":"AT-300-108","set":"AT-300","num":108,"question":"Examples of circumstances that may create self-review threat least\nlikely include","options":{"A":"preparation of original data used to generate financial statements\nor preparation of other records that are the subject matter of the\nassurance engagement","B":"a member of the assurance team being, or having recently been, an\nemployee of the assurance client in a position to exert direct and\nsignificant influence over the subject matter of the assurance\nengagement","C":"potential employment with an assurance client."},"correctAnswer":"C","topic":"Professional Ethics & Independence","standard":"Philippine Code of Ethics for Professional Accountants","rationale":"The Philippine Code of Ethics establishes five fundamental principles (Integrity, Objectivity, Professional Competence & Due Care, Confidentiality, and Professional Behavior) and a conceptual framework requiring CPAs to identify, evaluate, and address threats to compliance through appropriate safeguards.","distractorNotes":"Oth